            <ArticleTitle>Chronic clofibrate therapy in maintenance hemodialysis patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>21 hypertriglyceridemic hemodialysis patients were treated with 1--2 g/week of clofibrate. The dosage reduction from the usual clofibrate dose of 14 g/week avoided toxicity and corrected the abnormalities in serum triglyceride and high density lipoprotein cholesterol levels to or toward normal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
